le=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Otoh, I don't believe RAW it works. Otoh, I think one of the pieces of fluff have someone poisoning someone's candy on halloween?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mrs. Winters doesn't have Basilisk's Touch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T23:42:50-08:00","id":806807,"title":"","content":"As written, Basilisk's Touch isn't an ability that gives you access to poisons that can be applied in multiple ways. You have to touch the target with a touch attack. That said, I allow its use in non-combat situations if you make physical contact with an NPC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T09:25:14-08:00","id":807077,"title":"","content":"Huh. She doesn't? Then no, Basilisk's touch can not affect weapons. Honestly, that sort of makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T13:44:34-08:00","id":809822,"title":"","content":"How about if I &quot;attack&quot; the weapon first. RAW the weapon is poisoned.<br /> <br /> How about sap gloves?<br /> <br /> Also, RAW: <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Satiety Expenditure: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Venom drips from the Beast\u2019s <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">fingertips and greenish-black streaks course through the veins <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">of his arm as he reaches out with a concentrated dose of poison.</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Does it mean, I spend satiety and gain one venom dose?<br /> <br /> Also, the passive power means that RAW &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">The Beast\u2019s touch applies either the <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Drugged Tilt or the grave version of the Poisoned Tilt to the <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">victim.&quot; </span></span></span></span></span></span>No roll, no satiety expenditure, noting. Imagine a Vampire feeding from a Beast with this power. As a GM I would rule the vamp sucked poisoned / drugged vitae. Meaning, the blood is always poisoned. Than, again, one could poison a weapon with such blood.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10749-skydiver","name":"skydiver","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}